# The CI requirement set, as the hand-edited input. constraints-ci.txt is the
# lock generated from it: every distribution of the closure pinned with a
# sha256 hash for each file the index serves at that version. CI installs the
# lock with `python -m pip install --require-hashes -r constraints-ci.txt`
# (.github/workflows/tests.yml, .github/workflows/fast-tests.yml and
# .cursor/install.sh); scripts/verify_ci_environment.py checks the installed
# environment against it at runtime.
#
# The names below are the suite's direct dependencies plus pip, pinned to the
# TEST-phase-verified versions. Merge-time resolution is code execution in CI,
# so a version change is a reviewed change to this file and its lock, never
# merge-time weather. Transitive versions are fixed by the lock and change only
# through a refresh.
# Exact pins only (`name==version`, optional trailing comment).
#
# pip IS pinned. The install upgrades or downgrades pip to the pinned version
# inside the same hash-checked install. Measured 2026-11-12 on aarch64 Linux,
# CPython 3.12.3: 24.0 -> 26.3 and 26.2.2 -> 26.3 upgrade, and 26.3 -> 26.2.2
# downgrade, each rc 0 with every other package installed. The ubuntu-latest
# runner's setup-python shipped pip 26.2.2 at that date, below this pin.
#
# REFRESH, from the repository root, with the uv version the lock header names
# (a different uv version may write different bytes):
#   uvx uv@0.13.6 pip compile constraints-ci.in --generate-hashes \
#     --python-version 3.12 --python-platform x86_64-manylinux_2_28 \
#     --no-annotate --custom-compile-command \
#     "uvx uv@0.13.6 pip compile constraints-ci.in --generate-hashes --python-version 3.12 --python-platform x86_64-manylinux_2_28 --no-annotate -o constraints-ci.txt" \
#     -o constraints-ci.txt
# A refresh keeps every version the lock already holds. To move a transitive,
# add `--upgrade-package <name>`; to move everything, add `--upgrade`. Then run
# the suite green under the new lock and commit the .in and lock diff together.
# Measured 2026-11-12 with uv 0.13.6: a second compile of the same input is
# byte-identical, and the lock is byte-identical for Python 3.12, 3.13 and 3.14
# and for x86_64 and aarch64 Linux and both macOS targets. Every pinned
# version has an x86_64 manylinux wheel for CPython 3.12, 3.13 and 3.14, so CI
# builds nothing from source. Windows adds colorama and is not a CI platform.
#
# Incident path, a COMPROMISED TRANSITIVE: pin it here at a safe version and
# refresh; the lock and the verify script then hold it there.
#
# What CI does NOT certify: consumers never read this file. pact-memory's
# runtime install (skills/pact-memory/scripts/memory_init.py) runs a bare
# `pip install <pkg>`, so a consumer resolves the newest pysqlite3,
# sqlite-vec and model2vec the index serves. A breaking upstream release
# therefore reaches consumers while CI stays green on these pins; a refresh
# is the step that would surface it.
pip==26.3
pytest==9.2.0
hypothesis==6.170.14
httpx==0.28.1
pytest-asyncio==1.4.1
pytest-xdist==3.8.0
pyyaml==6.0.3
pysqlite3==0.6.1
sqlite-vec==0.1.9
model2vec==0.10.0
ruff==0.17.3
pytest-randomly==5.1.0
